{"name":"Harvester","hex":"#edc38e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"harvester","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who gathers the harvest (harvests the crop).","A machine that gathers the harvest (harvests the crop)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/harvester"}],"entries":[{"title":"Combine harvester","blocks":[{"text":"The modern combine harvester, also called a combine, is a machine designed to harvest a variety of cultivated seeds. Combine harvesters are one of the most economically important labour-saving inventions, significantly reducing the fraction of the population engaged in agriculture. Among the crops harvested with a combine are wheat, rice, oats, rye, barley, corn (maize), sorghum, millet, soybeans, flax (linseed), sunflowers and rapeseed (canola). The separated straw is then either chopped onto the field and ploughed back in, or laid out in rows, ready to be baled and used for bedding and cattle feed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Corn_combine_harvest_with_grain_cart-4.jpg/330px-Corn_combine_harvest_with_grain_cart-4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Combine_harvester","wikidata":"Q26886"},{"title":"Forage harvester","blocks":[{"text":"A forage harvester – also known as a silage harvester, forager or chopper – is a farm implement that harvests forage plants to make silage. Silage is grass, corn or hay, which has been chopped into small pieces, and compacted together in a storage silo, silage bunker, or in silage bags. It is then fermented to provide feed for livestock. Haylage is a similar process to silage but using grass which has dried."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Forage_harvester.jpg/330px-Forage_harvester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forage_harvester","wikidata":"Q1900188"},{"title":"Harvester (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Harvester is a point-and-click adventure game written and directed by Gilbert P. Austin and developed by DigiFX Interactive. It was published for MS-DOS, Windows, and Linux in North America on September 24, 1996. Players take the role of Steve Mason, an 18-year-old man who awakens in the fictional Texas town of Harvest in 1953, with amnesia. Over the next week, he is coerced or manipulated into performing a series of tasks with increasingly violent consequences at the behest of The Order of the Harvest Moon, a cult-like organization which seems to dominate the town and which promises to reveal the truth about Steve and how he found himself in Harvest. The game is known for its violent content and its meta-commentary examination of violence, and has garnered a cult following."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/4a/Harvester_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvester_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q549466"},{"title":"Harvester (restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"Harvester is a casual dining restaurant chain in the United Kingdom. The first, The George Inn, opened in 1983 in Morden, South London. The chain, set up by Courage Brewery to compete with Whitbread's Beefeater restaurants and Grand Metropolitan's Berni Inns, is currently run by Mitchells & Butlers. It serves burgers, salad, traditional British pub food and drinks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cf/Harvester_%28restaurant%29_logo.svg/330px-Harvester_%28restaurant%29_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harvester_(restaurant)","wikidata":"Q5676915"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Lely-M%C3%A4hdrescher.jpg/500px-Lely-M%C3%A4hdrescher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/Lely-M%C3%A4hdrescher.jpg/500px-Lely-M%C3%A4hdrescher.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Lely open-cab combine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALely-M%C3%A4hdrescher.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Old_Style_Harvester.jpg/500px-Old_Style_Harvester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Old_Style_Harvester.jpg/1280px-Old_Style_Harvester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Old_Style_Harvester.jpg/500px-Old_Style_Harvester.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A \"Sunshine\" harvester in the Henty, Australia, region","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOld_Style_Harvester.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Mules_pull_farm_equipment_%283537172980%29.jpg/500px-Mules_pull_farm_equipment_%283537172980%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Mules_pull_farm_equipment_%283537172980%29.jpg/1280px-Mules_pull_farm_equipment_%283537172980%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Mules_pull_farm_equipment_%283537172980%29.jpg/500px-Mules_pull_farm_equipment_%283537172980%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Case harvester, 20+ mule team","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMules_pull_farm_equipment_(3537172980).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/CaseCombineHarvester.jpg/500px-CaseCombineHarvester.jpg?ut